questiontext.text:
Given the following class definition and incomplete `main()` method:

    public class One {
        private int field = 0;

        One(int f) { field = f; }
        void change(int g) { field = g; }
        void add(One other) { field = field + other.field; }
    }

    public class Main {
        public static void main(String[] args) {
            // FIXME
        }
    }

Fill in the `main()` method, replacing the `FIXME` comment in its body, so that it creates an object of class `One` containing the value `15` and then changes the value stored in that object to a `5`.

**Note:** a 0% penalty regime applies. This means that you can click the `Check` button as much as time allows with no penalty.

question.answerpreload:
class Main {
  public static void main(String[] args) {
    // FIXME
  }
}

